<span class="section-num">16.</span>
<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew § 16</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה בְּחִינַת חֵטְא הַמְרַגְּלִים שֶׁנָּתַן לָהֶם ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ מָקוֹם לִטְעוֹת עַל שֶׁרָצוּ לַחֲקֹר יוֹתֵר מִדַּאי, כְּמוֹ שֶׁאָמְרוּ רַבּוֹתֵינוּ זַ"ל, אֲנִי אָמַרְתִּי לָהֶם שֶׁהִיא טוֹבָה וְהֵם לֹא רָצוּ לְהַאֲמִין וְכוּ', חַיֶּיךָ שֶׁאֲנִי נוֹתֵן לָהֶם מָקוֹם לִטְעוֹת וְכוּ'. כִּי אֶרֶץ יִשְׂרָאֵל הִיא עִקַּר בְּחִינַת אֱמוּנָה, כְּמוֹ שֶׁמְּבֹאָר בְּמָקוֹם אַחֵר וְהֵם רָצוּ לִרְאוֹת בְּעֵינֵיהֶם מִיָּד אֵיךְ בָּאִין לְאֶרֶץ יִשְׂרָאֵל. וְלֹא רָצוּ לִסְמֹךְ עַל אֱמוּנָה אַף-עַל-פִּי שֶׁכְּבָר רָאוּ אוֹתוֹת וּמוֹפְתִים נוֹרָאִים וְנִפְלָאִים כָּאֵלֶּה, אַף-עַל-פִּי-כֵן אָמְרוּ, נִשְׁלְחָה אֲנָשִׁים לְפָנֵינוּ וְיַחְפְּרוּ לָנוּ אֶת הָאָרֶץ וְכוּ'. כִּי רָצוּ לִרְאוֹת וּלְהָבִין הָאֱמֶת מִיָּד, עַל-כֵּן נָתַן לָהֶם ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ מָקוֹם לִטְעוֹת וְגָרְמוּ בְּכִיּוֹת לְדוֹרוֹת עַד הַיּוֹם שֶׁמִּתְאָרֵךְ הַגָּלוּת עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה. וְעִקַּר הַגְּאֻלָּה תְּלוּיָה בָּזֶה, כִּי כֵּן דֶּרֶךְ ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ שֶׁהוּא עוֹסֵק בְּרַחֲמָיו לְקָרֵב אֶת הָאָדָם בְּכַמָּה דְּרָכִים, אַךְ אַף-עַל-פִּי-כֵן הוּא מַנִּיחַ לוֹ מָקוֹם לְהִסְתַּפֵּק קְצָת בִּשְׁבִיל נִסָּיוֹן וּבְחִירָה. וּכְשֶׁמִּתְחַזֵּק בֶּאֱמוּנָה שְׁלֵמָה עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁמִּסְתַּכֵּל עַל הָאֱמֶת עַל כָּל הַחֲסָדִים שֶׁעָשָׂה ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ וְהֵאִיר בּוֹ מֵרָחוֹק רְמָזִים בְּכַמָּה דְּרָכִים לְהוֹדִיעוֹ הֵיכָן הָאֱמֶת בְּוַדַּאי יִזְכֶּה לְכָל טוֹב אֲמִתִּי וְנִצְחִי, אֲבָל אִם יִרְצֶה לְבַקֵּשׁ תּוֹאֲנוֹת לִפְרֹשׁ, נוֹתֵן לוֹ ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ מָקוֹם לִטְעוֹת יוֹתֵר וְיוֹתֵר וְצָרִיךְ אַחַר כָּךְ יְגִיעוֹת גְּדוֹלוֹת וַעֲצוּמוֹת מְאֹד בְּיוֹתֵר קֹדֶם שֶׁיִּזְכֶּה אֶל הָאֱמֶת וְכוּלֵי הַאי וְאוּלַי. עַד שֶׁיָּכוֹל לִפְטֹר מִן הָעוֹלָם וְלֹא יִזְכֶּה אֶל הָאֱמֶת וְיִצְטָרֵךְ לִסְבֹּל מַה שֶּׁיִּסְבֹּל וּלְהִתְגַּלְגֵּל בְּכַמָּה גִּלְגּוּלִים עַד שֶׁיָּבוֹא לְהִתְקָרֵב אֶל הָאֱמֶת, שֶׁהָיָה בְּיָדוֹ לִזְכּוֹת בּוֹ עַתָּה עַל-יְדֵי נִסָּיוֹן קַל לְהַשְׁלִיךְ תַּאֲוַת הַכָּבוֹד וְהַנִּצָּחוֹן וּלְהִסְתַּכֵּל עַל הָאֱמֶת לַאֲמִתּוֹ וְכַנַּ"ל: וְזֶה שֶׁהִקְפִּיד עֲלֵיהֶם ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ וְאָמַר לְמֹשֶׁה, עַד אָנָה יְנַאֲצֻנִי הָעָם הַזֶּה וְעַד אָנָה לֹא יַאֲמִינוּ בִּי בְּכָל הָאֹתוֹת אֲשֶׁר עָשִׂיתִי בְּקִרְבּוֹ. הַיְנוּ כַּנַּ"ל, כִּי הֲלֹא כְּבָר הִתְחַלְתִּי לְהָאִיר לָהֶם הָאֱמֶת עַל-יְדֵי כָּל הָאוֹתוֹת אֲשֶׁר עָשִׂיתִי בְּקִרְבָּם וַעֲדַיִן אֵינָם מַאֲמִינִים מֵחֲמַת הַקֻּשְׁיוֹת שֶׁלָּהֶם שֶׁרוֹצִים לְהָבִין וְלִרְאוֹת הַכֹּל מִיָּד וְכַנַּ"ל. עַל-כֵּן גָּזַר עֲלֵיהֶם אָז הַגָּלוּת וְהַחֻרְבָּן שֶׁנִּמְשָׁךְ עַד הֵנָּה שֶׁיִּצְטָרְכוּ לְהִתְנַסּוֹת בְּכָל דּוֹר וָדוֹר בְּעִנְיָן זֶה שֶׁמִּי שֶׁיִּרְצֶה לְהִסְתַּכֵּל עַל הָאֱמֶת עַל-יְדֵי כָּל מַה שֶּׁכְּבָר הִתְחִיל ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ לְהָאִיר בּוֹ, יוּכַל לְהָבִין הֵיכָן הָאֱמֶת וְיִתְחַזֵּק בֶּאֱמוּנָה עַל כָּל מַה שֶּׁאֵינוֹ יָכוֹל לְהָבִין וּלְהֵפֶךְ לְהֵפֶךְ כַּנַּ"ל. וּבָזֶה תְּלוּיָה עִקַּר הַגְּאֻלָּה, כִּי עִקַּר הַגְּאֻלָּה תְּלוּיָה בָּאֱמוּנָה, כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, תָּבוֹאִי תָּשׁוּרִי מֵרֹאשׁ אֲמָנָה, הַיְנוּ כַּנַּ"ל. וְהָבֵן הֵיטֵב אִם תִּרְצֶה לָחוּס עַל חַיֶּיךָ הַנִּצְחִיִּים:</div>

<p class="first">And this is the aspect of the <strong>sin of the <em>meraglim</em></strong>, that Hashem, blessed be He, gave them room to err, because they wanted to investigate more than was fitting. As our Sages of blessed memory said: <span class="verse-inline">"I told them that it is good, and they did not wish to believe"</span> etc. — <span class="verse-inline">"by your lives, I will give them room to err"</span> etc. For Eretz Yisra'ail is the primary aspect of <em>emunah</em>, as is explained elsewhere. And they wanted to see with their own eyes immediately how one comes to Eretz Yisra'ail. And they did not wish to rely on <em>emunah</em>, even though they had already seen such awesome and wondrous signs and wonders. Nevertheless, they said, <span class="verse-inline">"Let us send men before us, and let them search out the Land for us"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Deuteronomy 1:22)</span> etc. For they wanted to see and understand the <em>emes</em> immediately — therefore Hashem, blessed be He, gave them room to err, and they caused weeping for generations until this day, for the exile has been prolonged because of this.</p>

<p>And the primary redemption depends on this. For this is the way of Hashem, blessed be He: He engages in His mercy to draw a person close through many paths. But nevertheless, He leaves him room to have some doubt, for the sake of testing and <em>bechirah</em>. And when one strengthens himself in complete <em>emunah</em> — by looking at the <em>emes</em>, at all the kindnesses that Hashem, blessed be He, has done, and how He has illuminated for him from afar through hints in many ways to make known to him where the <em>emes</em> is — he will certainly merit all true and eternal good.</p>

<p>But if he wishes to seek pretexts to separate — Hashem, blessed be He, gives him room to err more and more, and he then needs very great and immense exertions before he merits the <em>emes</em> — and all this and perhaps. To the point that he can depart from the world and not merit the <em>emes</em>, and he will need to endure what he will endure and be reincarnated in numerous reincarnations until he comes to draw close to the <em>emes</em> — which he could have merited now through a minor test: to cast aside the desire for honor and competitiveness and to look at the <em>emes</em> in its truest sense, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is what Hashem, blessed be He, was angered at them and said to Moshe: <span class="verse-inline">"How long will this people provoke Me, and how long will they not believe in Me, with all the signs that I have performed in their midst?"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Numbers 14:11)</span>. That is, as mentioned above: I have already begun to illuminate for them the <em>emes</em> through all the signs that I performed in their midst, and still they do not believe, because of their questions — for they want to understand and see everything immediately, as mentioned above. Therefore He decreed upon them at that time the exile and the destruction that has continued until now — that they will need to be tested in every generation in this matter: that one who wishes to look at the <em>emes</em>, through all that Hashem, blessed be He, has already begun to illuminate in him, will be able to understand where the <em>emes</em> is, and will strengthen himself in <em>emunah</em> regarding all that he cannot understand. And the reverse, the reverse, as mentioned above. And on this the primary redemption depends. For the primary redemption depends on <em>emunah</em>, as it is written, <span class="verse-inline">"You shall come, you shall gaze, from the peak of <em>amanah</em>"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Song of Songs 4:8)</span>. That is, as mentioned above. And understand this well, if you wish to have compassion on your eternal life.</p>

